1
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:16,291
Come out of there!

2
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:32,333
<i>Phii Pong comes out at night</i>
<i>to hunt for its victims.</i>

3
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:35,250
<i>Once it catches its prey,</i>

4
00:01:35,333 --> 00:01:37,166
<i>it kills them,</i>

5
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:38,916
<i>then rips open the belly,</i>

6
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,416
<i>and pulls out the guts,</i>

7
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,333
<i>and eats their organs.</i>

8
00:01:42,416 --> 00:01:47,291
DELUSION

9
00:01:54,791 --> 00:01:58,333
If you see Phii Pong, then it must

10
00:01:58,416 --> 00:01:59,958
kill you straight away.

11
00:02:00,041 --> 00:02:02,083
Otherwise, it will die.

12
00:02:02,166 --> 00:02:03,875
After it kills you,

13
00:02:03,958 --> 00:02:06,083
then it starts to eat your guts.

14
00:02:07,375 --> 00:02:10,625
Wouldn't it get diarrhea after that?

15
00:02:11,666 --> 00:02:13,333
No. It's a ghost.

16
00:02:13,416 --> 00:02:14,791
Ah…

17
00:02:14,875 --> 00:02:17,500
But you said it turns into
a human in the morning.

18
00:02:17,583 --> 00:02:22,083
They say that near your mother's village,
Phii Pongs are everywhere.

19
00:02:22,166 --> 00:02:26,166
So, take care. You better watch yourself,
or you'll ger eaten.

20
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:35,708
- Wow.
- Oh look it's here!

21
00:02:35,791 --> 00:02:37,250
- Look at that.
- Beautiful.

22
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:38,375
Say, Wan.

23
00:02:38,875 --> 00:02:40,625
- Yeah?
- The food is delicious.

24
00:02:40,708 --> 00:02:44,875
Did you order it from Bangkok?
Yote said you arranged it all.

25
00:02:44,958 --> 00:02:46,333
Can I get their contact?

26
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:49,166
Of course you can, I'll text you.

27
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:52,958
Sunee is so lucky
to have you as her daughter-in-law.

28
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:57,041
So Wan, tell me, how are things with you?

29
00:02:57,958 --> 00:02:59,583
I'm doing well.

30
00:03:00,333 --> 00:03:03,291
You're so, you've been deputy, so long.

31
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,750
It's time you were school principal.

32
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:16,625
Excuse me, if you would.

33
00:03:16,708 --> 00:03:17,666
Of course, dear.

34
00:03:21,916 --> 00:03:23,291
Enough with the talking.

35
00:03:23,375 --> 00:03:26,250
- Enough with that! Time to have fun now.
- A bit for everyone.

36
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:28,041
Okay, raise your glasses, to all of us.

37
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:30,000
To all of us! Here we go.

38
00:03:30,083 --> 00:03:31,583
- Congratulations.
- Cheers.

39
00:03:31,666 --> 00:03:33,208
Mrs. Wan, this delivery is for you.

40
00:03:33,291 --> 00:03:34,500
I'll take care of it.

41
00:03:35,125 --> 00:03:36,791
Our client ordered more, ma'am.

42
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,125
CASH SALE
FIVE CASES OF CHAMPAGNE, 39,000 BAHT

43
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
- Okay, you can take it in.
- Yes ma'am.

44
00:03:50,083 --> 00:03:54,833
50TH ANNIVERSARY APPRECIATION BANQUET
KANG CHAI LIMITED PARTNERSHIP

45
00:03:54,916 --> 00:03:58,708
SPONSORED BY LOEI FORWARD GROUP

46
00:03:58,791 --> 00:04:00,000
- Cheers.
- Thank you so much.

47
00:04:00,083 --> 00:04:02,000
I'd like to thank you all for today.

48
00:04:02,083 --> 00:04:03,500
Thank you, cheers.

49
00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:35,041
You can go home if you like.

50
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,625
Aim can stay with me.

51
00:04:42,166 --> 00:04:43,541
You've been drinking.

52
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,375
I'm okay.

53
00:04:47,166 --> 00:04:49,583
He can stay with me tonight.

54
00:04:49,666 --> 00:04:51,333
You stay here.

55
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:55,708
My mom's expecting him to stay with us.

56
00:05:06,541 --> 00:05:08,208
Transfer it, when you can.

57
00:05:14,541 --> 00:05:16,333
That was my family's money anyway.

58
00:05:17,458 --> 00:05:20,208
Just think of it,
as you helping out for a change.

59
00:05:22,875 --> 00:05:23,833
Just this once.

60
00:05:25,875 --> 00:05:28,041
I've given plenty of money to your family.

61
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:29,333
This is small change.

62
00:05:47,791 --> 00:05:50,000
So, your grandparents had diarrhea?

63
00:05:50,083 --> 00:05:52,875
No, because my grandparents
aren't Phii Pongs.

64
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:56,083
Stay long enough, and you'll find out.

65
00:05:56,750 --> 00:06:00,666
Your grandparents will
be looking after you. Do you know why?

66
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:04,750
My mom says it's because
your parents are getting divorced.

67
00:06:04,833 --> 00:06:06,416
Hey!

68
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,875
Hey! What are you kids playing?
Hey, what are you up to?

69
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:10,583
What's going on here?

70
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:16,791
We've got lychees. Come on, nice dessert.

71
00:06:16,875 --> 00:06:18,833
- Oh! Yum!
- Let's go, good now.

72
00:06:18,916 --> 00:06:20,750
Okay, lychee time!

73
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,750
MOM

74
00:06:31,375 --> 00:06:32,958
Hello?

75
00:06:33,041 --> 00:06:34,166
What's up, Mom?

76
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:36,250
<i>Wan, you need to come</i>
<i>and talk to your dad.</i>

77
00:06:36,333 --> 00:06:39,750
<i>I don't know what's wrong, but he's gone</i>
<i>a bit funny. He's got a machete!</i>

78
00:06:40,291 --> 00:06:41,666
<i>What? Mom!</i>

79
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:42,750
<i>Mom!</i>

80
00:06:46,333 --> 00:06:47,500
Come out!

81
00:06:55,458 --> 00:06:57,375
I said come on out!

82
00:06:58,125 --> 00:07:00,250
Ma? Ma?

83
00:07:00,333 --> 00:07:02,125
<i>- Mom!</i>
- Hey!

84
00:07:04,875 --> 00:07:05,916
Ma?

85
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,375
Ma?

86
00:07:07,458 --> 00:07:08,416
Ma!

87
00:07:12,250 --> 00:07:14,250
WAN

88
00:07:18,625 --> 00:07:20,625
FOUR MISSED CALLS

89
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:39,041
50TH ANNIVERSARY APPRECIATION BANQUET

90
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,041
Aim.

91
00:08:01,125 --> 00:08:02,250
Come on, we're going.

92
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:04,041
- You've gotta go?
- Okay, see you.

93
00:08:04,125 --> 00:08:05,750
- Bye.
- Bye.

94
00:08:05,833 --> 00:08:07,500
Goodbye, Aunt Wan.

95
00:08:30,708 --> 00:08:31,875
What's up, Wan?

96
00:08:32,375 --> 00:08:34,083
<i>It's Dad, there's something wrong.</i>

97
00:08:34,166 --> 00:08:35,791
<i>What? What's wrong?</i>

98
00:08:35,875 --> 00:08:37,666
<i>Doctor, the patient is prepped.</i>

99
00:08:38,208 --> 00:08:40,250
<i>Look, I'm with a patient right now.</i>

100
00:08:40,333 --> 00:08:42,750
<i>Can you…Can you handle this?</i>
<i>For the moment.</i>

101
00:08:51,791 --> 00:08:54,083
You can sleep, we're not there yet.

102
00:08:57,500 --> 00:09:02,041
Ma, I would have been all right alone.
I'm old enough now.

103
00:09:05,583 --> 00:09:06,875
Yeah, but…

104
00:09:07,375 --> 00:09:09,833
Who would keep me company? Hmm?

105
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:14,000
Grandpa's house is so boring.

106
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:15,833
There's never anything to do.

107
00:09:16,416 --> 00:09:18,250
And it's hot, no AC.

108
00:09:19,291 --> 00:09:21,208
No, it's not hot at all.

109
00:09:21,291 --> 00:09:22,833
It's always cool there.

110
00:09:22,916 --> 00:09:26,000
There are so many nice trees
and it's shady.

111
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,500
Trees aren't the same as AC

112
00:09:40,458 --> 00:09:44,791
NASAO VILLAGE NASAO, CHIANG KHAN, LOEI

113
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:48,791
CHIANG KHAN POLICE STATION

114
00:09:48,875 --> 00:09:50,500
POLICE MAJOR SASIDIT DESAYAKUL

115
00:09:52,791 --> 00:09:56,500
INVESTIGATION DIVISION
CHIANG KHAN POLICE STATION

116
00:09:56,583 --> 00:09:58,833
CAPT. BIRD: I HEARD YOU MOVED
TO CHIANG KHAN, PETE

117
00:09:58,916 --> 00:10:00,500
I'M HERE WITH MY BOSS. LET'S MEET UP.

118
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:06,208
Hey, Uncle, are you going to
the village party this week?

119
00:10:06,916 --> 00:10:09,125
I don't think so, not really my thing.

120
00:10:10,583 --> 00:10:11,666
Huh?

121
00:10:12,333 --> 00:10:14,583
It sounded like a lot of fun.

122
00:10:14,666 --> 00:10:16,458
- There'll be lots of free beer.
- Mmm.

123
00:10:19,416 --> 00:10:21,541
I'm bored. Feel like a smoke?

124
00:10:21,625 --> 00:10:22,791
Okay, yeah, let's go.

125
00:10:24,125 --> 00:10:25,500
Got a spare ticket.

126
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,375
If you want it.

127
00:10:31,416 --> 00:10:32,250
Sure.

128
00:10:33,958 --> 00:10:36,458
- Let's go.
- The missing person case, any updates?

129
00:10:40,083 --> 00:10:42,833
The one the old lady came in to report.

130
00:10:43,333 --> 00:10:46,208
Oh yeah, um, he…

131
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:49,791
Uh, he probably already showed up.

132
00:10:49,875 --> 00:10:53,000
Probably just, got drunk or
passed out somewhere.

133
00:10:53,083 --> 00:10:54,625
You know that for a fact, do you?

134
00:10:54,708 --> 00:10:55,750
Uh…

135
00:10:56,875 --> 00:10:58,500
The kid is 16, right?

136
00:10:58,583 --> 00:11:00,250
Yeah, here sir.

137
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:05,125
The kid's name is Mued.
He's Grannie Paew's grandson.

138
00:11:05,208 --> 00:11:07,666
And he's been missing
for over 24 hours now.

139
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,708
You know where they live?

140
00:11:10,875 --> 00:11:11,875
Yeah.

141
00:11:11,958 --> 00:11:13,083
Good.

142
00:11:13,583 --> 00:11:16,250
Take me there,
I'll wait for you out front.

143
00:11:18,541 --> 00:11:20,250
You said it.

144
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:23,416
- Yeah, so much for a smoke, eh?
- Yeah.

145
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,125
- Let's go.
- I'm coming, I'm coming.

146
00:11:41,041 --> 00:11:42,750
Hey! What are you doing there?

147
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:44,291
You're Grandpa-Rong, are you?

148
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,166
Grannie Paew!

149
00:11:50,416 --> 00:11:52,708
Are you there, Grannie Paew?

150
00:11:52,791 --> 00:11:53,916
The police are here.

151
00:11:59,958 --> 00:12:02,916
Oh! You take care now.
Careful, let me help you.

152
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,666
Have you found him?

153
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:05,916
They haven't yet.

154
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,416
This police officer is here
to help us look.

155
00:12:15,416 --> 00:12:17,416
MUED

156
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:23,333
It's a scarecrow, keeps ghosts away.

157
00:12:23,833 --> 00:12:26,375
They put that out,
if there's a male in the house.

158
00:12:26,458 --> 00:12:28,500
Stops ghosts from taking them.

159
00:12:29,041 --> 00:12:30,750
It's pretty common around here.

160
00:12:44,708 --> 00:12:45,791
Grannie.

161
00:12:45,875 --> 00:12:48,625
Where does the boy sleep?
Can I see please?

162
00:13:03,875 --> 00:13:05,708
Come on in, Officer.

163
00:13:17,125 --> 00:13:19,125
Where are your grandson's things?

164
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:47,833
He doesn't go to school?

165
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:52,583
He hasn't been to school
for over a year now.

166
00:13:56,375 --> 00:13:58,791
Is there anything missing of value?

167
00:13:58,875 --> 00:14:00,458
No, nothing.

168
00:14:00,541 --> 00:14:03,208
Before he left,
he even left some money for me.

169
00:14:10,125 --> 00:14:12,541
Where did he get that money from?

170
00:14:13,958 --> 00:14:15,416
What do you see, Sergeant?

171
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:17,333
Tracks could be his.

172
00:14:19,291 --> 00:14:21,875
- Tracks, inspector
- Check the kid's motorbike.

173
00:14:21,958 --> 00:14:23,958
They don't remember the license plate.

174
00:14:24,041 --> 00:14:26,666
Whatever you find out,
notify our patrol unit

175
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:28,375
and the other stations as well.

176
00:14:28,875 --> 00:14:29,708
Sir.

177
00:14:32,833 --> 00:14:36,041
Are the kids around here
in a local bike gang?

178
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,666
Where do they hang out?

179
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:39,708
I think they…

180
00:14:39,791 --> 00:14:42,541
buy their booze at the local store
and then they go

181
00:14:42,625 --> 00:14:45,875
- and drink it on the farms.
- Not in the forest?

182
00:14:47,666 --> 00:14:51,208
No one would dare go
poking around in the forest, Officer.

183
00:14:51,291 --> 00:14:54,958
There's Phii Pong there,
everyone's too afraid.

184
00:14:55,041 --> 00:14:57,875
A ghost will catch you and eat you.

185
00:14:57,958 --> 00:14:59,291
What ghost?

186
00:14:59,375 --> 00:15:00,833
Phii Pong.

187
00:15:00,916 --> 00:15:04,333
It hunts in the forest
for frogs and toads to eat.

188
00:15:05,083 --> 00:15:07,583
Or it'll rip out your guts and eat them.

189
00:15:07,666 --> 00:15:09,625
Tomorrow the shaman's going to perform

190
00:15:09,708 --> 00:15:13,833
a ritual which will exorcise the ghost.
You should come along.

191
00:15:13,916 --> 00:15:15,250
Everyone will be here.

192
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:22,708
Let me go! Let me go!
Where are you taking me?

193
00:15:22,791 --> 00:15:25,125
Hey! What's going on there?

194
00:15:25,708 --> 00:15:28,791
He's possessed again.
We'll take him to the shaman.

195
00:15:32,666 --> 00:15:33,708
What's going on?

196
00:15:33,791 --> 00:15:35,041
I want to go home.

197
00:15:35,958 --> 00:15:39,208
He's a police officer,
he's here to help find the boy.

198
00:15:39,291 --> 00:15:40,708
It took you long enough.

199
00:15:40,791 --> 00:15:42,458
This is the ghost who's eaten him!

200
00:15:42,541 --> 00:15:45,000
The boy went missing
after he was possessed.

201
00:15:45,625 --> 00:15:46,833
Narong!

202
00:15:46,916 --> 00:15:50,708
What did you do to my grandson?
Where did you take him to?

203
00:15:54,625 --> 00:15:55,500
Uncle.

204
00:15:56,166 --> 00:15:58,583
My name's Pete, I'm a new officer here.

205
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:01,625
Can you tell me whose blood
is that on your shirt?

206
00:16:03,875 --> 00:16:06,375
He won't answer you, Officer.
He's Phii Pong.

207
00:16:06,458 --> 00:16:08,333
You should just lock him up.

208
00:16:11,375 --> 00:16:13,708
Just to be clear, you two didn't hurt him?

209
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:17,958
You didn't beat him up just
because you think he's Phii Pong.

210
00:16:18,041 --> 00:16:19,916
That would be an offense.

211
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,416
It's my blood.

212
00:16:25,041 --> 00:16:26,916
I was using a knife.

213
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,416
I cut myself.

214
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:30,083
He was trying to help me.

215
00:16:30,166 --> 00:16:32,000
So he ran off to get assistance.

216
00:16:33,958 --> 00:16:36,708
He didn't go for help.
He just ran into the forest.

217
00:16:36,791 --> 00:16:38,833
Your husband's a ghost! He was hunting.

218
00:16:38,916 --> 00:16:40,541
There are no ghosts here.

219
00:16:43,125 --> 00:16:44,875
That's an amulet you're wearing, isn't it?

220
00:16:46,416 --> 00:16:48,791
Ghosts can't be close to amulets,
can they?

221
00:16:53,166 --> 00:16:54,791
You two live together, is that right?

222
00:16:57,208 --> 00:17:00,375
Let's get you to a doctor, I'll drive you.

223
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,791
It's not a deep wound,
I'll be fine, thank you.

224
00:17:03,875 --> 00:17:05,958
I'd like to help.

225
00:17:06,041 --> 00:17:08,250
Let me drive you to the hospital now.

226
00:17:08,333 --> 00:17:09,833
We'll get him checked out, too.

227
00:17:46,041 --> 00:17:47,125
What's going on, Auntie?

228
00:17:47,208 --> 00:17:50,125
It's your dad, he's been possessed.

229
00:17:59,833 --> 00:18:02,083
Hospitals have germs, go wash your hands.

230
00:18:02,166 --> 00:18:03,000
Okay.

231
00:18:08,708 --> 00:18:10,000
I'm their daughter.

232
00:18:10,083 --> 00:18:11,333
My name is Wan.

233
00:18:11,916 --> 00:18:14,083
We're seeing to your mother's wound now.

234
00:18:14,166 --> 00:18:16,166
- As for your father…
- His name is Narong.

235
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,875
Yes, the doctor on duty is assessing him.
I'll let you know when there's an update.

236
00:18:23,416 --> 00:18:24,291
Good evening.

237
00:18:28,708 --> 00:18:30,291
Are you their daughter?

238
00:18:31,416 --> 00:18:32,666
Yes.

239
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:34,750
Wanrudee.

240
00:18:37,041 --> 00:18:39,500
How long as your father been like this?

241
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,375
Not long.

242
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:48,041
But you don't live with them, do you?

243
00:18:48,541 --> 00:18:50,125
So how can you be sure?

244
00:18:50,208 --> 00:18:53,625
The neighbors say
he's been like this for a while now.

245
00:18:53,708 --> 00:18:55,583
I visit them regularly.

246
00:18:55,666 --> 00:18:57,375
I don't just leave them alone.

247
00:18:57,458 --> 00:19:00,125
He was perfectly fine
the last time I saw him.

248
00:19:00,208 --> 00:19:02,000
How long ago was that then?

249
00:19:02,875 --> 00:19:05,291
A neurological condition could be serious.

250
00:19:05,375 --> 00:19:07,833
I think that's for the doctor to decide.

251
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:11,708
I'm not sure that
you're qualified to know.

252
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,083
Am I wrong?

253
00:19:16,666 --> 00:19:17,791
That's fair.

254
00:19:17,875 --> 00:19:20,916
If you don't mind,
I'd like you to give this to your father.

255
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,416
There are things
I'd like to discuss with him…

256
00:19:24,125 --> 00:19:26,416
Once the doctor
has finished his examination.

257
00:19:28,958 --> 00:19:30,958
POLICE MAJOR SASIDIT DESAYAKUL

258
00:19:32,166 --> 00:19:34,500
If my dad's done something illegal,

259
00:19:34,583 --> 00:19:36,166
then please tell me.

260
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:39,708
As it stands,
no one has filed a complaint.

261
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,458
I do find your mother's wound
somewhat odd.

262
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,458
Speaking as a policeman.

263
00:19:45,541 --> 00:19:49,416
Let me go! Let go!
Why did you bring me here?

264
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:52,291
- Let me go! Take your hands off me!
- Please calm down.

265
00:19:52,375 --> 00:19:55,958
What medicine?
I'm not taking any medicine! I'm not sick!

266
00:19:56,041 --> 00:19:58,833
You're all in on this together,
aren't you?

267
00:19:58,916 --> 00:20:01,833
- You're trying to take my land off me!
- Please, sir!

268
00:20:01,916 --> 00:20:06,291
- You're trying to take what's mine!
- We're trying to help you!

269
00:20:08,375 --> 00:20:10,625
Based on my assessment of the patient,

270
00:20:10,708 --> 00:20:13,375
he's beginning to show
the early signs of dementia.

271
00:20:14,416 --> 00:20:20,458
Even his agitated behavior
and his constant talk of the past,

272
00:20:20,541 --> 00:20:24,750
it seems he's become fixated
on these memories he has.

273
00:20:25,791 --> 00:20:27,041
So…

274
00:20:27,875 --> 00:20:29,541
How is this treated?

275
00:20:30,208 --> 00:20:31,416
I should start

276
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:34,833
by telling you that there's
no treatment for this condition.

277
00:20:34,916 --> 00:20:38,750
The medication I'm prescribing
will only help slow its progression,

278
00:20:38,833 --> 00:20:41,458
so the symptoms don't worsen too quickly.

279
00:20:42,083 --> 00:20:43,500
But frankly speaking,

280
00:20:43,583 --> 00:20:47,208
your family needs to consider that
he will require constant care.

281
00:20:48,583 --> 00:20:52,791
Indeed, in the future,
he may need 24 hour professional care.

282
00:20:52,875 --> 00:20:54,833
I'll admit him for tonight and tomorrow.

283
00:20:54,916 --> 00:20:57,708
You can take him home once he's awake.

284
00:20:59,125 --> 00:21:01,208
EXAMINATION ROOM

285
00:21:03,375 --> 00:21:05,375
YOTE

286
00:21:08,208 --> 00:21:10,333
- Hello.
- <i>Where did you take Aim?</i>

287
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,166
<i>I told you he was staying with me tonight.</i>

288
00:21:13,250 --> 00:21:15,500
<i>Are you too stupid to understand that?</i>

289
00:21:16,958 --> 00:21:20,833
<i>From now on, you need to tell me</i>
<i>before you take him anywhere, understand?</i>

290
00:21:21,583 --> 00:21:23,791
<i>Are you listening to me? Wan!</i>

291
00:21:23,875 --> 00:21:25,750
<i>Can you hear me? Hello?</i>

292
00:21:26,708 --> 00:21:27,541
<i>Bit--</i>

293
00:21:57,833 --> 00:21:59,750
He has medicine to take after breakfast.

294
00:21:59,833 --> 00:22:01,250
I'll leave it here for you.

295
00:22:03,666 --> 00:22:06,458
Ma, let me clean that up,
you go get some sleep.

296
00:22:08,125 --> 00:22:10,083
It's better if I do it.

297
00:22:21,791 --> 00:22:23,208
So, Dad did that?

298
00:22:28,708 --> 00:22:30,958
I don't know what it was he saw.

299
00:22:31,791 --> 00:22:35,541
He tried to kill me. Who knows…

300
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:38,208
What it is that's wrong with him.

301
00:22:38,291 --> 00:22:40,916
Perhaps it was a spirit?

302
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:44,041
Maybe something blew in and took over him.

303
00:22:44,666 --> 00:22:46,250
Where's the machete?

304
00:22:47,708 --> 00:22:49,166
I took it, and hid it.

305
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:52,750
How long has he been like this?

306
00:22:59,833 --> 00:23:00,791
Ma.

307
00:23:04,083 --> 00:23:06,375
The doctor said Dad is very sick.

308
00:23:08,291 --> 00:23:10,291
It has nothing to do with any ghosts.

309
00:23:11,666 --> 00:23:16,041
What would a doctor know?
I live with your father every day.

310
00:23:16,125 --> 00:23:19,833
He wouldn't do that to me,
if he wasn't possessed.

311
00:23:23,083 --> 00:23:24,291
You go to bed.

312
00:23:28,125 --> 00:23:30,583
Is it time to charge that tablet?
What do you think?

313
00:23:45,375 --> 00:23:46,208
Ma.

314
00:23:46,291 --> 00:23:48,000
What's wrong with Grandpa?

315
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:51,541
Why was he shouting like that?

316
00:23:53,625 --> 00:23:55,125
Grandpa's sick.

317
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:58,791
And we don't know what it is.

318
00:24:00,583 --> 00:24:02,666
But, will he get better?

319
00:24:04,333 --> 00:24:05,333
Mmm-mmm.

320
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:08,416
Mmm.

321
00:24:09,875 --> 00:24:10,750
Ma…

322
00:24:11,833 --> 00:24:13,500
Do you think that…

323
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,166
Phii Pong is a real thing?

324
00:24:16,958 --> 00:24:18,500
It's silly.

325
00:24:19,250 --> 00:24:20,916
It's all nonsense.

326
00:24:22,958 --> 00:24:25,000
Well, some people say it's true.

327
00:24:25,583 --> 00:24:27,000
Well, they're wrong.

328
00:24:28,208 --> 00:24:29,833
They're all just silly stories, see.

329
00:24:31,125 --> 00:24:32,208
Listen to me.

330
00:24:33,083 --> 00:24:36,791
The people who say that,
they haven't actually seen anything.

331
00:24:38,083 --> 00:24:39,666
- Right?
- Mmm.

332
00:24:39,750 --> 00:24:40,583
They haven't.

333
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:42,833
Okay.

334
00:24:44,750 --> 00:24:45,666
Yeah.

335
00:24:52,125 --> 00:24:53,458
- Ma.
- Hmm?

336
00:24:53,541 --> 00:24:55,250
Don't forget to brush your teeth.

337
00:24:55,333 --> 00:24:57,375
I left the toothpaste out.

338
00:25:04,291 --> 00:25:05,375
What's funny?

339
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:08,083
I think you're growing a moustache.

340
00:25:09,333 --> 00:25:10,166
Hmm?

341
00:25:12,458 --> 00:25:14,208
Yes, I can see it.

342
00:25:14,291 --> 00:25:17,125
Look, it's so thick!
I think you need to shave!

343
00:25:17,208 --> 00:25:18,666
I don't have a moustache!

344
00:25:18,750 --> 00:25:19,791
I don't!

345
00:25:19,875 --> 00:25:21,875
Stop it! stop it!

346
00:25:21,958 --> 00:25:23,541
Oh, that tickles!

347
00:25:23,625 --> 00:25:25,416
It tickles! Ah!

348
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:28,041
What did you forget? Hmm?

349
00:25:28,666 --> 00:25:33,458
Good night! Have a sweet dream.

350
00:25:34,375 --> 00:25:39,083
Thank you, Teacher Wan.

351
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:42,916
Good night.

352
00:25:44,541 --> 00:25:45,833
- Night.
- You have sweet dreams.

353
00:26:04,750 --> 00:26:08,625
Behold,

354
00:26:08,708 --> 00:26:12,625
O gods and celestial beings.

355
00:26:13,208 --> 00:26:18,666
You who abide in every tree
and mountain-wood,

356
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:22,541
in every deep forest and wilderness,

357
00:26:22,625 --> 00:26:27,416
in all rivers, pools, and fish-bays.

358
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:32,291
Gather, all you hosts of deities.

359
00:27:00,208 --> 00:27:01,708
My grandson.

360
00:27:01,791 --> 00:27:05,416
Let the ghost free you, come back to me.

361
00:27:21,291 --> 00:27:23,416
Get out! Gone! Be gone!

362
00:27:23,500 --> 00:27:26,041
Gone! Be gone!

363
00:27:26,125 --> 00:27:28,833
Be gone! Be gone!

364
00:27:28,916 --> 00:27:35,750
Go! Get out!

365
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:39,666
- Get out!
- Be gone!

366
00:27:39,750 --> 00:27:44,833
- Get out!
- Be gone! Get out!

367
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,000
FAMILY WAITING AREA

368
00:28:21,750 --> 00:28:23,708
You still like liquid diabetes?

369
00:28:25,250 --> 00:28:26,791
Don't joke around, Wat.

370
00:28:35,583 --> 00:28:37,708
So, how long has he been in there?

371
00:28:38,625 --> 00:28:39,916
A while now.

372
00:28:42,708 --> 00:28:45,500
It's just a CT scan.

373
00:28:45,583 --> 00:28:46,833
It shouldn't be too long.

374
00:28:49,541 --> 00:28:51,208
How's Mom doing?

375
00:28:54,333 --> 00:28:55,916
Her wound is healing.

376
00:28:57,916 --> 00:29:00,208
Wat…if you're free…

377
00:29:01,041 --> 00:29:02,333
You should go and see her.

378
00:29:04,375 --> 00:29:05,375
Yeah, I will.

379
00:29:05,958 --> 00:29:07,541
I swapped shifts.

380
00:29:11,208 --> 00:29:13,208
If these drugs don't work.

381
00:29:14,083 --> 00:29:16,958
I think we should seriously consider…

382
00:29:17,750 --> 00:29:19,958
shifting him to a care center.

383
00:29:20,041 --> 00:29:21,750
We can't take care of him on our own.

384
00:29:21,833 --> 00:29:24,125
Let's see if the drugs work.

385
00:29:24,208 --> 00:29:26,166
I don't want him abandoned.

386
00:29:27,166 --> 00:29:28,708
For someone else to look after.

387
00:29:32,083 --> 00:29:33,208
Can you manage alone?

388
00:29:33,291 --> 00:29:35,083
I'll have to, won't I?

389
00:29:35,750 --> 00:29:37,833
I've managed so far without you.

390
00:29:52,708 --> 00:29:53,541
Pa.

391
00:29:55,041 --> 00:29:57,166
Your father's condition has improved.

392
00:29:57,250 --> 00:29:59,000
He should be fine.

393
00:29:59,083 --> 00:30:02,708
But if any symptom return
once he's at home,

394
00:30:02,791 --> 00:30:05,458
Please, feel free to contact us any time.

395
00:30:05,541 --> 00:30:06,791
Thanks very much, I will.

396
00:30:24,083 --> 00:30:29,333
I, proclaiming the four noble truths,
they obtained blessed victory

397
00:30:29,416 --> 00:30:35,416
may these victories of the glorious dharma
and the sangha

398
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:39,083
be bestowed upon those who chant
and those who heal.

399
00:30:40,750 --> 00:30:42,291
And now fill it up.

400
00:30:44,416 --> 00:30:47,041
Beware of what the wind brings in.

401
00:30:47,708 --> 00:30:51,250
We live close to the forest,
and to the mountains.

402
00:30:52,291 --> 00:30:57,541
If you hear anything in the night,
do not heed it and do not say a word.

403
00:30:57,625 --> 00:31:02,708
And keep your mind steady,
say your prayers before you retire.

404
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:14,666
Get out, get out!

405
00:31:14,750 --> 00:31:18,041
Be gone! Get out! Come on!

406
00:31:18,125 --> 00:31:22,500
- Get out!
- Be gone!

407
00:31:22,583 --> 00:31:29,166
- Get out!
- Be gone!

408
00:31:37,541 --> 00:31:39,458
- Let's go!
- Be gone!

409
00:31:44,541 --> 00:31:45,833
Get out! Get out!

410
00:31:45,916 --> 00:31:48,375
- Get out!
- Be gone!

411
00:31:48,458 --> 00:31:50,541
Get out!

412
00:31:51,666 --> 00:31:52,625
Open the gate, kid.

413
00:31:55,125 --> 00:31:56,750
Get out! Be gone!

414
00:31:56,833 --> 00:32:00,291
- Get out!
- Get out!

415
00:32:02,833 --> 00:32:07,375
- Get out!
- Get out!

416
00:32:09,083 --> 00:32:10,416
Do you live here?

417
00:32:11,458 --> 00:32:12,625
Mmm-hmm.

418
00:32:12,708 --> 00:32:14,958
There is a ghost here in your house.

419
00:32:17,375 --> 00:32:19,416
- That's wrong.
- Your grandpa's a Phii Pong.

420
00:32:19,500 --> 00:32:24,041
- Phii Pong! Be gone!
- Be gone! Get out!

421
00:32:30,666 --> 00:32:33,125
- Get out!
- Go away!

422
00:32:35,583 --> 00:32:38,333
- Get out!
- Be gone!

423
00:32:52,958 --> 00:32:56,166
<i>Sadhu. Sadhu. Sadhu.</i>

424
00:32:56,250 --> 00:33:00,000
Spirits of
the land, mountains, forests, and city.

425
00:33:00,083 --> 00:33:03,666
If our children who became lost
in the forest or the town

426
00:33:03,750 --> 00:33:08,875
have unintentionally offended you,
by body, mind, or speech,

427
00:33:08,958 --> 00:33:15,583
I humbly ask for your forgiveness.

428
00:33:15,666 --> 00:33:18,458
Please open the gates,

429
00:33:18,541 --> 00:33:22,541
and show them the way,

430
00:33:22,625 --> 00:33:25,666
and protect them

431
00:33:25,750 --> 00:33:29,833
from harm, danger, or misfortune.

432
00:33:29,916 --> 00:33:34,083
Open the way.

433
00:33:59,291 --> 00:34:01,541
- Come on, let's go home.
- Yeah.

434
00:34:58,291 --> 00:35:01,000
Aw, you caught me.

435
00:35:01,083 --> 00:35:02,083
Uncle Wat!

436
00:35:02,166 --> 00:35:04,750
Hi there Aim, what's up?

437
00:35:05,500 --> 00:35:08,250
I came to see what this was all about.

438
00:35:08,333 --> 00:35:09,375
Hmm.

439
00:35:10,875 --> 00:35:12,958
They do some strange shit around here.

440
00:35:13,041 --> 00:35:14,875
Not like in the city.

441
00:35:16,541 --> 00:35:17,541
Did they scare you?

442
00:35:19,958 --> 00:35:22,333
Come on, mosquitoes are biting.

443
00:35:22,416 --> 00:35:24,708
- Okay.
- Yeah, let's go.

444
00:36:39,791 --> 00:36:41,208
Where could it be?

445
00:36:49,541 --> 00:36:51,291
Yes, that's right. Sit here.

446
00:36:58,458 --> 00:36:59,291
Here.

447
00:37:05,708 --> 00:37:08,708
Yay! Look, I got one! You go, Grandpa!

448
00:37:10,708 --> 00:37:11,833
Uh…

449
00:37:12,958 --> 00:37:13,875
That's it!

450
00:37:19,208 --> 00:37:20,041
You're close.

451
00:37:20,125 --> 00:37:21,000
Here.

452
00:37:21,500 --> 00:37:22,875
Let me help.

453
00:37:23,416 --> 00:37:24,333
Yeah!

454
00:37:28,958 --> 00:37:30,125
There you go.

455
00:37:30,750 --> 00:37:32,041
Caught 'em…

456
00:37:32,125 --> 00:37:34,708
Yay! You did it, good one!

457
00:37:35,708 --> 00:37:36,708
Great!

458
00:38:05,541 --> 00:38:07,500
Grandpa, what's wrong?

459
00:38:07,583 --> 00:38:08,416
Grandpa?

460
00:38:14,916 --> 00:38:16,791
Grandpa, don't cry.

461
00:38:20,750 --> 00:38:22,541
Go, you keep playing…

462
00:39:10,083 --> 00:39:13,291
<i>What time will you drop him?</i>
<i>He has taekwondo class tomorrow.</i>

463
00:39:13,375 --> 00:39:15,916
He'll be there in time for that.

464
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:19,541
<i>I'm coming to get him now, so he can sleep</i>
<i>in and not have to wake up early.</i>

465
00:39:19,625 --> 00:39:22,083
Why do you want to do that?

466
00:39:22,166 --> 00:39:24,250
He'll already be asleep by then.

467
00:39:27,166 --> 00:39:29,625
I know what's best for my son.

468
00:39:30,750 --> 00:39:32,625
I think you should consider that.

469
00:39:33,125 --> 00:39:35,333
<i>What the fuck are you trying to say, huh?</i>

470
00:39:35,416 --> 00:39:36,791
<i>Wan--</i>

471
00:42:28,250 --> 00:42:29,416
Ma?

472
00:42:29,500 --> 00:42:31,041
Ma!

473
00:42:32,333 --> 00:42:33,375
Ma!

474
00:45:16,041 --> 00:45:17,333
Hey!

475
00:45:22,708 --> 00:45:25,166
Grandpa! Grandpa!

476
00:45:26,250 --> 00:45:27,333
Grandpa?

477
00:45:28,708 --> 00:45:30,000
Grandpa!

478
00:52:26,250 --> 00:52:31,250
Subtitle translation by: Parida Kim
